r"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/successors","kind":"symbol","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.Successors","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Successors","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure’s row for one vertex, each target checked to be a vertex as it is read (not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the row is formed). A struct rather than a lazy map, so an algorithm that keeps an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator per vertex on its stack (Tarjan’s) allocates nothing for it."}]}}}